# Wren Gallery, for story pictures, the scene camera and music fades: the easel puts three pictures up and takes one down
# by name, cuts the camera to a cell and then moves it to a marker over a second and a half, and plays a track with its own
# fade and then cut; the window sends the camera back to the leader, plays a track with game.json's fade, takes the top
# picture down, clears the rest, shows a last one and warps within the gallery, which resets the camera and keeps the
# picture.

event gallery_easel skippable
	picture show harbor_dawn
	narrate @gallery.easel.dawn
	picture show storm
	picture show beacon
	narrate @gallery.easel.storm
	picture hide storm
	camera to 8 3
	music play title_harbor_dawn fade 800
	narrate @gallery.easel.beacon
	music play title_harbor_dawn cut
	camera to window_front 1.5 nowait
end

event gallery_window skippable
	camera reset 0.5
	music play field_marsh_reeds
	narrate @gallery.window.view
	picture hide
	picture clear
	picture show farewell
	narrate @gallery.window.farewell
	camera to far_corner 2 nowait
	warp wren_gallery gallery_door
end
